  "title": "o1 model with date-stamped versions fails since they don't support `'system'`",
  "url": "https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/issues/2179",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2024-10-29T00:33:03Z",
  "closed_at": "2024-10-29T20:03:36Z",
  "body": "### Issue\n\nWhile attempting to use the `azure/o1-preview-2024-09-12` model, I encountered the following error:\r\n```\r\nlitellm.BadRequestError: AzureException BadRequestError - Error code: 400 - {'error': {'message': \"Unsupported value: \r\n'messages[0].role' does not support 'system' with this model.\", 'type': 'invalid_request_error', 'param': \r\n'messages[0].role', 'code': 'unsupported_value'}}\r\n```\r\nThis issue is likely to occur with other date-stamped versions of the o1 model as well.\r\n\r\nThis issue is related to the following issues:\r\n\r\n- #1521, and\r\n- #1581.\r\n\r\n\r\nIt appears that non-date-stamped models have already addressed in commits such as 8aee4d25ed6de2fb6c624edaf8f5c9674e511532. However, this fix has not been applied to date-stamped versions of the o1 model.\n\n### Version and model info\n\nAider: [current latest development version](https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/tree/ed4ad45e3d7114d129eff32afcd260044ea07fdb)",
